  "texts": {
   "ladder": "the response of the original is the smallest ladder of so(4,2) (premise T' / I_pos read on the real form): ladder_gates then gives positivity, a continuous positive time and Weyl dimension 3 + 1",
   "equilibrium": "entanglement equilibrium of the seam state (premise D, Jacobson): Einstein dynamics with the area coefficient of the state",
   "irreducible": "the Hardy compression of the seam is an irreducible isometry (Z30) or the ground state carries the twist (premise G)",
   "vacuum": "the state on an observer's diamond is the vacuum of a local net (Bisognano-Wichmann, Hislop-Longo)",
   "index_kms": "the even modular response normalises I beta c3 = 1 (open bridge of P1.INDEX.KMS.01)",
   "cone_gravitates": "the replica cone of the purity gravitates: tension (n-1)/(4n) with G = 1",
   "family_is_twistor": "the three family directions lie in the conformal algebra su(2,2) of the seam's twistor space, and the A3 factor of E8 (ledger SEL.THM.01) is that algebra: with compact Spin(10) the real form is E8(-24), fields are representations of (Spin(10) x SU(2,2))/Z4, and the Z4 rule of z4_gates gives one chiral generation with a single orientation bit.  Tested on 27 November (w5, family_clock_gates): the square of the family clock has the signature of the Cartan involution of su(2,2) and of no other real form of A3; in the ledger dictionary H^0(K(D)) the families are the so(2,1) of the seam line with the clock -Ad(rho4).  Refuted in the earlier form 'family directions = Cartan of su(2,2) with the clock rho4': as a Weyl element the family clock is of Coxeter class",
   "oriented_state": "the world state is the oriented state of the seam and not the SU(2,2)-invariant vacuum; its helicity phase is c3 phi0, with the sign of the orientation bit"
  }
 },
